repository-code: "https://github.com/Project-Navi/navi-creative-determinant"
url: "https://projectnavi.ai"
abstract: >-
  The Creative Determinant (CD) framework models autopoietic closure as a
  nonlinear elliptic boundary value problem on a compact Riemannian manifold.
  A finite-graph positive-existence theorem with an explicit example, and the
  algebraic and order-theoretic lemmas, are machine-checked in Lean 4 against
  Mathlib; the continuum existence theorems are formalized conditionally on an
  analytic interface (`PDEInfra`) and proved classically in the paper. The
  framework combines the mathematics (elliptic PDEs, fixed-point theorems)
  with enactivist and semiotic foundations and an empirical layer (the CD
  condition and its falsifiability criteria).
keywords:
